{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Trolley Problem in AI.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Trolley Problem in AI.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"trolley problem in ai trolley problem in ai","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Trolley Problem in AI.md","fileName":"Trolley Problem in AI.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Trolley Problem in AI","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Machine Moral Status]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Functional Morality","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Trolley Problem in AI.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Trolley Problem in AI.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"trolley problem in ai trolley problem in ai","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Trolley Problem in AI.md","fileName":"Trolley Problem in AI.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Trolley Problem in AI","heading":"Trolley Problem in AI","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"The trolley problem in AI applies a forced-choice moral dilemma to an autonomous system, often asking how a self-driving vehicle should distribute unavoidable harm. It is useful for revealing conflicts among principles and for asking who is authorized to encode a choice.\n\nIts artificial simplicity can misrepresent real engineering. Actual safety decisions involve uncertain perception, probabilities, design trade-offs, maintenance, law, and opportunities to prevent the dangerous situation before a final collision choice exists. Ethical design should therefore not reduce [[Functional Morality]] to selecting a victim in a stylized scenario.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Functional Morality","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Trolley Problem in AI.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Trolley Problem in AI.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"trolley problem in ai trolley problem in ai","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Trolley Problem in AI.md","fileName":"Trolley Problem in AI.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Trolley Problem in AI","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiethics.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Machine Moral Status","Functional Morality","aiethics.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}